     9	//! header, so its `float_t` resolves to `<math.h>`'s `float_t` (== `float` on
    10	//! x86-64 glibc). The two translation units therefore disagree about the
    11	//! element type, and the compiled library really does behave that way. See
    12	//! `spectral_contrast.rs` for details.
