1. [1mNaN destination-operand roles were reversed in three places.[22m GCC at [38;5;10m-O0[0m emits [38;5;10maddsd %xmm1,%xmm0[0m with the [3mfreshly loaded[23m value as the destination and the accumulator as the source, and [38;5;10mmulss %xmm1,%xmm0[0m with [38;5;10mb[i][0m as the destination. SSE resolves a two-NaN operand pair in favour of the destination, so the Rust returned the wrong NaN payload from [38;5;10mtotal[0m, [38;5;10msmoothen[0m and [38;5;10mdot_product[0m. Because [38;5;10mspectral_contrast[0m re-reads those [38;5;10mdouble[0ms as [38;5;10mfloat[0m lanes, a wrong payload changes the [3mlane values[23m, which flips [38;5;10mmatch[0m's [38;5;10mint[0m return — not just a cosmetic bit pattern. Fixed in [38;5;10mtotal[0m, [38;5;10msmoothen[0m, [38;5;10mdot_product[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
2. [1m[38;5;10mslice::from_raw_parts[0m in the exported wrappers.[22m On a [38;5;10mNULL[0m pointer with a positive length the C segfaults; Rust's precondition check turned that into [38;5;10mSIGABRT[0m. The wrappers now walk raw pointers, matching both the fault and the "non-positive length dereferences nothing" behaviour.[0m[0m
